  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nWith the cold front now pushing further southeast and out of the\narea, a period of dry conditions is expected. Ensembles still \nshow some variation in conditions between a trough dug into the \nCanadian Maritimes, a warm and wet airmass over the SE CONUS and\nthe large amplitude central CONUS ridge. However, the most \nlikely scenario keeps us on the eastern fringe of the ridge in a\nnorthwest flow regime promoting drier and cooler weather late \nweek through the weekend. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nThe Monday through Wednesday timeframe will feature the\npotential of weakening/shifting of the ridge over the region.\nAlthough temperatures appear to be right around normal, there \nis a potential of afternoon showers and thunderstorms developing\non the edges of the ridge in the eastern ridges on Monday and \nTuesday. By Wednesday, another shortwave crossing the area will \nallow the ridges to weaken a bit more with a slightly higher \narea of coverage. These precip chances will be diurnal and \nwidely scattered.",
